Doom for Inferno — build plan
=============================

Goal: run shareware Doom (doom1.wad) under hosted emu, engine rewritten
in Limbo.  Reference spec: doomgeneric's 5-function platform seam
(DG_Init, DG_DrawFrame, DG_SleepMs, DG_GetTicksMs, DG_GetKey) — we port
the seam to Inferno and translate the engine body C -> Limbo.  Target:
a full, vanilla-faithful E1 episode playthrough (monsters fight back,
doors open, exit works, status bar/HUD present, SFX audible).

Build / run
-----------
  build   cd /home/steve/inferno-os/appl/doom && \
          PATH=/home/steve/inferno-os/Linux/386/bin:$PATH mk install
  run     cd /home/steve/inferno-os && DISPLAY=:0 \
          ./Linux/386/bin/emu /dis/doom/doom.dis doom1.wad
  modes   Run through ~/bin/emu-audio (adds -c 1 JIT + the OSS
          audio bridge; -c 1 needs the emu/Linux segflush mprotect).
          doom [-v] [-R] [-w] [-g] [-p] [doom.wad]; -v enables sprite/
          masked diagnostics on stdout; -p prints frame timing
          (tic/render/convert/present avg+max) every 70 tics; F1
          snapshots a frame log, F2 reviews the last ~105 frames
          frozen (Left/Right step, F1 captures, F2/Esc resumes);
          no flag = play E1M4 (skill hardcoded MEDIUM);
          -w = IDKFA test loadout, -g = god mode (pre-M25 hooks)

Platform services available in-tree (verified):
  blit      Draw->Image.writepixels(dst, r, data), module/draw.m:190;
            data must match the screen's native format — hosted emu
            is 32bpp XRGB32 (emu/port/win-x11a.c forces depth 32)
  screen    Display.allocate(nil) then draw/writepixels on
            display.image (appl/cmd/wish.b path); no Tk, no wm needed
  clock     Sys->millisec(), Sys->sleep(), module/sys.m:141,153
  keys      /dev/scancode raw keycodes (press = code, release =
            code|0x80) via kbdreader -> buffered event chan
  pointer   /dev/pointer (mouse) — unused so far (milestone 25)
  audio     /dev/audio + /dev/audioctl, enc pcm, rate 11025
            (emu/port/audio-tbls.c — exactly Doom's SFX rate)

Layout
------
  wad.m/wad.b      WAD container loader (module, reusable)
  video.m/video.b  XRGB32 framebuffer -> emu screen blit (module)
  rend.m/rend.b    renderer: palette, colormap, flats, textures,
                   vanilla column/span drawers (module)
  map.m/map.b      map geometry: vertices, sectors, sides, lines,
                   things as adts; shared ref Sectors (module)
  view.m/view.b    world-view renderer: BSP walk, seg clip, wall
                   columns, two-sided upper/lower (module)
  info.m/info.b    generated state/mobj tables (geninfo.py; do not
                   re-read to "verify")
  game.m/game.b    play simulation: tic loop, movement, collision,
                   thinkers (module)
  doom.b           main command: input, main loop, present
  doom1.wad        shareware IWAD (data, place in $ROOT or pass path)
  PLAN             this file
  PLAN.done        historical close-out log for milestones 1-7

  planned (added by milestones below):
  sound.m/sound.b  SFX engine (17; no-op stub lands in 9)
  spr              sprite asset side lives in rend.b or a new module
                   — decide at milestone 8

